# Attaching a comprobante straight from Google Drive.
#
# All three values are PUBLIC — they ship inside the JavaScript the browser
# downloads, and they are meant to. None of them grants access to anything on
# their own: what a file costs is the user's own consent, given per file in
# Google's picker. There is no client secret here because there is no
# server-side exchange to protect; see src/lib/googleDrive.ts.
#
# Leave them unset and the "Desde Google Drive" button simply does not appear,
# which is the right state for a deploy that has no Google project behind it.
#
# To fill them in, at https://console.cloud.google.com/ :
#
#   1. Create a project (or pick one), then enable both the "Google Picker API"
#      and the "Google Drive API".
#   2. OAuth consent screen: External. Add the scope
#      .../auth/drive.file — the narrow one, which sees only the files a user
#      picks. Add yourself under Test users; that is what lets you use it
#      before Google has verified the app.
#   3. Credentials → OAuth client ID → Web application. Under "Authorized
#      JavaScript origins" list every origin Lindero is opened from:
#      http://localhost:5173 for dev, plus the real https:// address of the
#      droplet. An origin that is missing here fails at the consent popup.
#   4. Credentials → API key. Restrict it to the same origins (HTTP referrers)
#      and to the Picker API, so a copy of it lifted from the page is worth
#      nothing anywhere else.
#   5. The app ID is the project NUMBER, on the project's dashboard. With the
#      drive.file scope it is what ties the permission the picker grants to
#      this app — without it the file is chosen and the download then 404s.
#
# Until step 2's verification is done, the consent screen warns that the app is
# unverified. Expected: click "Advanced" → "Go to Lindero". It only has to be
# resolved before people outside the test-user list can use this.

# Real values go in .env, never here — this file is committed.

VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_GOOGLE_API_KEY=
VITE_GOOGLE_APP_ID=
